{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/8r2crj","slideIndex":3,"text":"With permission, photos can be sent to Tripo, an external AI service, to create a candidate 3D model. A person must review it because AI may invent unseen details. A language model proposes a short reply and an action; our application validates it and maps allowed actions to existing animation. Three.js renders the character, and a separate service provides synthetic speech. The owner may also ask AI to organize a memory. Matching excerpts are shown, but the owner must check the draft. The project uses external pretrained models; it did not train a foundation model."}
